<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The entitlements file for a machine whose Apple Developer team
	cannot register the iCloud container `iCloud.sh.mateo.empo`. Point
	`EMPO_ENTITLEMENTS` at this file in your own Signing.xcconfig. See
	Signing.xcconfig.example.

	The dict stays empty, and it must not become a missing file. A
	build with no entitlements file at all signs with no entitlements
	blob, and a naive resigner then synthesizes an incomplete one that
	breaks the document picker. Empo.entitlements carries the same
	note.

	The iCloud target hides itself at runtime here, per SPEC 9.1: with
	no entitlement the container URL is nil, the gate closes, and the
	add flow drops the iCloud entry.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
